Uh, well, I'm not recommending that you adopt the "take 'em alive" strategy
in that situation. It's not supposed to be easy...
The scene as described would probably have to be rendered as follows:

The goblin hits!
#grab
In which direction? {direction of goblin}
You seize the goblin and attempt to put it in your pack (more)
The goblin is too heavy for you to lift! (more)
The goblin swings its large black knife (more)
etc.

Oh, if you want a practical application of this move, how about:
You're on the run from an angry shopkeeper, when your path is blocked by
a newt. Instead of killing it, you pick it up, throw it towards the 'keeper,
then engrave the E-word and continue on your way. Voila! E-word blocks newt,
newt blocks 'keeper, and you're safe (for a while anyway). I'm sure other
uses could be found.

